.TH MASTOTEST 1
.SH NAME
mastotest \- test the #C/curl/JSON path masto(1) depends on
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mastotest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Mastotest
calls
.IR masto (1)'s
own in-process
.B pubtest()
seam, the same pattern
.IR bskytest (1)
uses against Bluesky (see that command's own man page for the
justification, which applies here unchanged).
.B Pubtest
fetches
.BR api/v1/instance ,
a real, public, unauthenticated endpoint every Mastodon server
exposes (a server description, not a session), through the exact
.B curl()
and JSON-decoding path
.BR masto (1)'s
own
.B timeline()
uses, and checks that the decoded
.B title
field is present. Because the endpoint needs no access token, this
exercises the whole transport \(em
.BR #C ,
the host's
.IR curl (1),
real TLS, and this tree's
.B json
library reading the reply back \(em without a credentials file.
.PP
.B Htmltest
checks
.BR masto (1)'s
own
.B detag()
against a table of HTML fragment / expected plain text pairs \(em a
pure function, so this needs no network. It is what caught a real
bug while this was being built: stripping
.B <br>
and
.B </p>
with no replacement glued adjacent words together
(\c
.B "line1<br>line2"
detagged straight to
.BR line1line2 ),
now fixed by treating those two tags as line separators (see
.IR masto (1)).
.PP
.B Feedtest
calls
.BR masto (1)'s
own
.BR decode() ,
the status-array walk
.BR timeline() 's
curl call hands off to, directly with a hand-built JSON array in the
real
.B api/v1/timelines/home
response shape \(em four statuses covering a normal one (with HTML
content and an
.B <br>
line break), one with no
.BR account ,
and one with no
.B content
\(em and checks the decoded lines against the expected text, in the
API's own order. This is a pure function, so it needs no network.
.PP
Exits with
.B PASS
or
.B FAIL
naming what the decoded response actually held.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/mastotest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR masto (1),
.IR bskytest (1)
.SH BUGS
.B Pubtest
needs real outbound network access to
.BR mastodon.social ;
offline or firewalled hosts will see curl itself fail there, not a
bug in the code under test.
.B Htmltest
and
.B feedtest
need no network but cover only the fixture cases built into them, not
every shape the real API can return.
